+## Why
+
+Services need to change stored and exchanged JSON documents with standard patches rather than ad-hoc code. RFC 6902 (JSON Patch) is the published standard, and it builds on the JSON Pointer support the library already has.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `applyPatch(document, patch)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, applying an RFC 6902 patch with the operations `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy` and `test`.
+- The result is a new value; the input document and patch are never mutated.
+- An invalid patch or a failing operation throws an error, and no partial result is returned.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `json-patch`: applying an RFC 6902 JSON Patch to a JSON document.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- New module `src/patch.ts` with tests, and a new export in `src/index.ts`.
+- Reuses the pointer parsing of `src/pointer.ts`; no change to the `json-pointer` requirements.
+- No new dependencies.
