+## ADDED Requirements
+
+### Requirement: Patch is applied to a document without mutation
+Applying a patch SHALL return the resulting document as a new value. The input document and the patch SHALL NOT be modified, and the result SHALL NOT share any object or array with the input document or the patch. Operations SHALL be applied in order, each to the result of the previous one. An empty patch SHALL return a copy of the document.
+
+#### Scenario: Input untouched
+- **WHEN** the patch `[{"op":"add","path":"/a/b","value":1}]` is applied to `{"a":{}}`
+- **THEN** `{"a":{"b":1}}` is returned and the input document is still `{"a":{}}`
+
+#### Scenario: Value from the patch is not shared
+- **WHEN** an `add` operation inserts an object value and the returned document is then modified
+- **THEN** the object in the patch is unchanged
+
+#### Scenario: Sequential operations
+- **WHEN** the patch adds `/a` and then replaces `/a`
+- **THEN** the second operation sees the value added by the first
+
+### Requirement: Invalid patches and failing operations are errors
+The patch SHALL be an array of operation objects. An error SHALL be thrown when the patch is not an array, when an element is not an object, when `op` is missing or not one of the six operation names, when `path` is missing or not a valid JSON Pointer, when `value` is missing for `add`, `replace` or `test`, or when `from` is missing or not a valid JSON Pointer for `move` and `copy`. An error SHALL also be thrown when an operation fails as described below. When an error is thrown no result is returned, and the input is left unmodified.
+
+#### Scenario: Unknown operation
+- **WHEN** an operation has `op` set to `"merge"`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Missing value
+- **WHEN** an `add` operation has no `value` member
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Null value is present
+- **WHEN** an `add` operation has `"value": null`
+- **THEN** `null` is added
+
+#### Scenario: Patch is not an array
+- **WHEN** the patch is an object
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Later operation fails
+- **WHEN** the second of two operations fails
+- **THEN** an error is thrown and the input document is unmodified
+
+### Requirement: add
+`add` SHALL insert `value` at `path`. For an object parent, it SHALL add the member, or replace it if it already exists. For an array parent, it SHALL insert the value before the given index, shifting later elements, where the index is between 0 and the array length inclusive; the token `-` SHALL append. The parent of `path` MUST exist, otherwise an error is thrown, as it is for an index past the array length or an index that is not a canonical array index. With the empty path, the value SHALL replace the whole document.
+
+#### Scenario: Add member
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"add","path":"/baz","value":"qux"}` is applied to `{"foo":"bar"}`
+- **THEN** `{"foo":"bar","baz":"qux"}` is returned
+
+#### Scenario: Insert into array
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"add","path":"/foo/1","value":"qux"}` is applied to `{"foo":["bar","baz"]}`
+- **THEN** `{"foo":["bar","qux","baz"]}` is returned
+
+#### Scenario: Append to array
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"add","path":"/foo/-","value":"x"}` is applied to `{"foo":["bar"]}`
+- **THEN** `{"foo":["bar","x"]}` is returned
+
+#### Scenario: Add replaces existing member
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"add","path":"/a","value":2}` is applied to `{"a":1}`
+- **THEN** `{"a":2}` is returned
+
+#### Scenario: Missing parent
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"add","path":"/baz/bat","value":"qux"}` is applied to `{"foo":"bar"}`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Index past the end
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"add","path":"/foo/3","value":"x"}` is applied to `{"foo":["a","b"]}`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Replace whole document
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"add","path":"","value":[1]}` is applied to any document
+- **THEN** `[1]` is returned
+
+#### Scenario: Special member names
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"add","path":"/__proto__","value":1}` is applied to `{}`
+- **THEN** the result has an own member named `__proto__` with value `1`, and no prototype is altered
+
+### Requirement: remove
+`remove` SHALL delete the value at `path`. The target MUST exist, otherwise an error is thrown. Removing an array element SHALL shift later elements down. The token `-` SHALL NOT be a valid target. With the empty path, the result SHALL be `null`.
+
+#### Scenario: Remove member
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"remove","path":"/baz"}` is applied to `{"baz":"qux","foo":"bar"}`
+- **THEN** `{"foo":"bar"}` is returned
+
+#### Scenario: Remove array element
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"remove","path":"/foo/1"}` is applied to `{"foo":["bar","qux","baz"]}`
+- **THEN** `{"foo":["bar","baz"]}` is returned
+
+#### Scenario: Remove missing target
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"remove","path":"/b"}` is applied to `{"a":1}`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: replace
+`replace` SHALL replace the value at `path` with `value`. The target MUST exist, otherwise an error is thrown, and `-` SHALL NOT be a valid target. With the empty path, the value SHALL replace the whole document.
+
+#### Scenario: Replace member
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"replace","path":"/baz","value":"boo"}` is applied to `{"baz":"qux","foo":"bar"}`
+- **THEN** `{"baz":"boo","foo":"bar"}` is returned
+
+#### Scenario: Replace missing target
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"replace","path":"/b","value":1}` is applied to `{"a":1}`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: move
+`move` SHALL remove the value at `from` and add it at `path`, as `remove` followed by `add`. The `from` location MUST exist, otherwise an error is thrown. An error SHALL be thrown when `from` is a proper prefix of `path` (a location cannot be moved into one of its children). Moving a location to itself SHALL leave the document unchanged.
+
+#### Scenario: Move member
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"move","from":"/foo/waldo","path":"/qux/thud"}` is applied to `{"foo":{"bar":"baz","waldo":"fred"},"qux":{"corge":"grault"}}`
+- **THEN** `{"foo":{"bar":"baz"},"qux":{"corge":"grault","thud":"fred"}}` is returned
+
+#### Scenario: Move array element
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"move","from":"/foo/1","path":"/foo/3"}` is applied to `{"foo":["all","grass","cows","eat"]}`
+- **THEN** `{"foo":["all","cows","eat","grass"]}` is returned
+
+#### Scenario: Move into own child
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"move","from":"/a","path":"/a/b"}` is applied to `{"a":{}}`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Move from missing location
+- **WHEN** `from` does not exist
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+### Requirement: copy
+`copy` SHALL add at `path` a copy of the value at `from`. The `from` location MUST exist, otherwise an error is thrown. The copy SHALL be independent of the original.
+
+#### Scenario: Copy member
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"copy","from":"/foo/waldo","path":"/qux/thud"}` is applied to `{"foo":{"bar":"baz","waldo":"fred"},"qux":{"corge":"grault"}}`
+- **THEN** `thud` is added to `qux` with value `"fred"` and `foo` is unchanged
+
+#### Scenario: Copy is independent
+- **WHEN** an object is copied and the copy is then changed by a later operation
+- **THEN** the original is unchanged
+
+### Requirement: test
+`test` SHALL succeed, leaving the document unchanged, when the value at `path` equals `value`, and SHALL otherwise throw an error. The target MUST exist. Equality is by JSON value: strings compare by code units, numbers by numeric value, objects when they have the same member names with equal values regardless of member order, arrays when they have the same length and equal elements in order, and values of different types are never equal. With the empty path, the whole document is compared.
+
+#### Scenario: Equal values
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"test","path":"/a","value":{"y":2,"x":1}}` is applied to `{"a":{"x":1,"y":2}}`
+- **THEN** the document is returned unchanged
+
+#### Scenario: Different values
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"test","path":"/a","value":"1"}` is applied to `{"a":1}`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Missing target
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"test","path":"/b","value":null}` is applied to `{"a":1}`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Array order matters
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"test","path":"/a","value":[2,1]}` is applied to `{"a":[1,2]}`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
